# Syncthing in-progress transfer files. They appear anywhere in the tree, are
# byte-identical to the file they shadow, and are pure noise in `git status` — one
# was accidentally committed to PR #49 by a `git add -A <dir>`.
.syncthing.*

# Syncthing CONFLICT copies — a different filename shape from the line above, and
# therefore not caught by it: `<name>.sync-conflict-<date>-<time>-<deviceid>.<ext>`.
#
# These are worse than the in-progress files, not merely more of them. An in-progress
# file is byte-identical to what it shadows; a conflict copy is by definition a
# DIFFERENT version of it. One found on 2026-08-07 was a generated
# `docs/rusticprofile.1` built from 0.1.31, sitting beside the real 0.2.2 one — so
# committing it by accident would put a stale man page in the tree under a name that
# reads as authoritative.
#
# It also blocked a release: `cargo publish` refuses on an unclean working directory,
# and an untracked file counts, so `just publish` failed until it was deleted by hand.
*.sync-conflict-*
